# HammerspoonSDK

The framework that [Hammerspoon 2](https://github.com/@APP_REPO@) extensions are
built against, as a Swift package. Each version of this package is the SDK from the Hammerspoon 2
release with the same version number, and is published automatically when that release is.

Use it to build an extension without Hammerspoon 2 installed, for example in CI. With Hammerspoon
2 installed, you can also build against its own copy of the framework, in
`/Applications/Hammerspoon 2.app/Contents/Frameworks`.

```swift
dependencies: [
    .package(url: "https://github.com/@PACKAGE_REPO@", from: "@VERSION@"),
],
```

Depend on the oldest version of Hammerspoon 2 you want your extension to work with: it can only
use the API that version's SDK has. Link the framework, but never embed it in your extension:
Hammerspoon 2 provides it, and refuses extensions that bring their own copy.

See the Extensions guide in the [Hammerspoon 2 documentation](https://cmsj.github.io/Hammerspoon2/)
for how to write, build and sign an extension, and
[Examples/ExtensionTemplate](https://github.com/@APP_REPO@/tree/@VERSION@/Examples/ExtensionTemplate)
for a starting point.
